        "finding": "The CPU uses half-pixel centers. Normalized divides by per-axis display size; Uniform centers the coordinates, divides by the larger display axis and multiplies by two."
      },
      {
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/blender/blender/02f0899d78e374b63e7181d9061e1f7ab03419cc/source/blender/compositor/shaders/compositor_image_coordinates_uniform.glsl",
        "finding": "The GPU Uniform shader expresses the same ordered arithmetic as the CPU. Compiler reciprocal lowering can produce small Float32 rounding differences; the port records exact differences and bounded errors separately."
      },
